# oracle: min_style hftn on a six-atom chain with harmonic bonds and angles and a Lennard-Jones pair term (1-4 pairs scaled), every iteration printed (the first six iterations: beyond them the rows differ from native only by rounding amplified by the finite-difference Hessian products, which grows about tenfold per iteration from the last-bit differences of the forces)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.1e-10, atoms 2.9e-9.
# oracle-inputs: w225cm_hftn_mol.data
units           real
atom_style      molecular
boundary        f f f
read_data       w225cm_hftn_mol.data
pair_style      lj/cut 4.0
pair_coeff      * * 0.1 3.0
special_bonds   lj 0.0 0.5 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 300.0 1.5
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 50.0 110.0
thermo          1
thermo_style    custom step pe fmax
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
min_style       hftn
minimize        1.0e-12 1.0e-10 6 3000
